[{:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-106447"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041015/assets/4ac7f5cd3405e3839b829edc19c440c973521a0263f1aaa0a2f8245697779561.png)\n\nWhich of the following sets of parametric equations, defined for $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),$ generate the parabola shown above?" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-84819/selection/75cd34de47770482d209cc6d0c4a90bf1632afd85d673742ad694785d337568a" :answer/id #uuid "d80fe1bd-97bd-5de8-bcf7-9febea4261cd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x-2=\\frac{1}{2}t,\\,y+2=\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-84819/selection/ada20bfa83b670eb15f8071bddf0ac53c0afe235200b5e5c193fb4bcec4c4b01" :answer/id #uuid "859997d3-a529-5cab-a1c7-76920df6f3de" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x-2=\\frac{1}{2}t,\\,y+2=\\frac{1}{4}{t}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-84819/selection/e899cd74bbc5cdba1e3f3fd8fa5580c79162167c20eff28afe24f97a5b343209" :answer/id #uuid "912c272a-14e2-5247-bd7e-23ee7b3ae2e7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x+2=\\frac{1}{4}t,\\,y-2=\\frac{1}{4}{t}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-84819/selection/dcd00355df821c8dc74dda457b4f292382075c5b20a6e38db89426f33d29bbe5" :answer/id #uuid "c5566a4d-7138-557e-b675-c0824617b854" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x+2=\\frac{1}{4}t,\\,y-2=\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-84819/selection/143b183a9d65dadacb9f7c09d65f742014c287713f56de4e054727da8e4c5b7e" :answer/id #uuid "e1e61765-b80b-504d-9903-e65e40eb0e8c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x-2=\\frac{1}{4}t,\\,y+2=\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-84819/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "190ef792-c922-5d09-9b81-5dfb13cfb364" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-84819/selection/ada20bfa83b670eb15f8071bddf0ac53c0afe235200b5e5c193fb4bcec4c4b01" :answer-field/choices ["q-84819/selection/75cd34de47770482d209cc6d0c4a90bf1632afd85d673742ad694785d337568a" "q-84819/selection/ada20bfa83b670eb15f8071bddf0ac53c0afe235200b5e5c193fb4bcec4c4b01" "q-84819/selection/e899cd74bbc5cdba1e3f3fd8fa5580c79162167c20eff28afe24f97a5b343209" "q-84819/selection/dcd00355df821c8dc74dda457b4f292382075c5b20a6e38db89426f33d29bbe5" "q-84819/selection/143b183a9d65dadacb9f7c09d65f742014c287713f56de4e054727da8e4c5b7e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-84819" :question/id #uuid "1250f77b-d8f7-59d3-9273-1f7c3e0a3b34" :question/math-academy-id "q-84819" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041015/assets/d963d5620df91a05c8371ef09beeb84546c5f5a8cda047f2c2c3b9933f3d5c01.png)\n\nWhich of the following sets of parametric equations, defined for $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),$ generate the parabola shown above?" :question/worked-solution "The diagram shows that the parabola is vertical, has its vertex at $(2,-2),$ and passes through the point $(4,2).$\n\nThe parametric equations of a vertical parabola that has its vertex at $(h,k)$ are\n\n$$\nx-h=2pt,\\,y-k=p{t}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is constant.\n\nIn our case, $(h,k)=(2,-2),$ and so we have\n\n$$\nx-2=2pt,\\,y+2=p{t}^{2}.\n$$\n\nSince the parabola passes through $(4,2),$ we can substitute $x=4$ and $y=2$ into the parametric equations to obtain a system of equations. This gives\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2=2pt \\\\ 4=p{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the first equation for $t,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 & =2pt \\\\ 1 & =pt \\\\ t & =\\frac{1}{p}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the second equation and solving for $p,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4 & =p{(\\frac{1}{p})}^{2} \\\\ 4 & =p\\cdot \\frac{1}{{p}^{2}} \\\\ 4 & =\\frac{1}{p} \\\\ p & =\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the parabola are\n\n$$\nx-2=2(\\frac{1}{4})t,\\,y+2=(\\frac{1}{4}){t}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhich simplify to\n\n$$\nx-2=\\frac{1}{2}t,\\,y+2=\\frac{1}{4}{t}^{2}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-84819/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "61e9c047-0bbf-560d-b803-87703164db5b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-84819"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-84828/selection/a4041a2026ac719066e48e5053b2b0e227cfb4bff49159aeba4556ed7298fa9f" :answer/id #uuid "62683e27-9171-5d90-bde1-8be606ab07d4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x-1=2t,\\,y-3=2{t}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-84828/selection/55a9aed18600d01cf9282532a9efcb1912a42c98c1a000355e6406ec15daee25" :answer/id #uuid "d4ee5ddc-90cc-5e13-8422-546f3e0b2696" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x-1=2t,\\,y-3={t}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-84828/selection/6d9d41c2d19a0659c448fde9138edc5db5adb4ac9510627696e21e88bcbd51cf" :answer/id #uuid "8f2cc450-47d9-525c-b902-ff52165199bf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x-1=-2t,\\,y-3=-{t}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-84828/selection/9937815e8c09805f8d4e65bbcab7dccf37008b483d8b917d0d395c42ca4b78c1" :answer/id #uuid "906738ad-407b-570a-8047-fbc4a1ef44c4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x+1=-2t,\\,y+3=-{t}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-84828/selection/9b0a3bb1de13ff4351ff7381797dfd88851af2f97ccf2a0241bc719104d5dc6f" :answer/id #uuid "6dd44e27-2480-5ca2-8900-037e49846439" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x+1=2t,\\,y+3={t}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-84828/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "13f3662d-5e8e-5a85-9562-de183a36299b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-84828/selection/55a9aed18600d01cf9282532a9efcb1912a42c98c1a000355e6406ec15daee25" :answer-field/choices ["q-84828/selection/a4041a2026ac719066e48e5053b2b0e227cfb4bff49159aeba4556ed7298fa9f" "q-84828/selection/55a9aed18600d01cf9282532a9efcb1912a42c98c1a000355e6406ec15daee25" "q-84828/selection/6d9d41c2d19a0659c448fde9138edc5db5adb4ac9510627696e21e88bcbd51cf" "q-84828/selection/9937815e8c09805f8d4e65bbcab7dccf37008b483d8b917d0d395c42ca4b78c1" "q-84828/selection/9b0a3bb1de13ff4351ff7381797dfd88851af2f97ccf2a0241bc719104d5dc6f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-84828" :question/id #uuid "09777cff-2521-5a71-be45-4262e5697b5e" :question/math-academy-id "q-84828" :question/problem "Which of the following sets of parametric equations, defined for $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),$ generate a vertical parabola that has its vertex at $(1,3)$ and which passes through the point $(-1,4)?$" :question/worked-solution "The parametric equations of a vertical parabola that has its vertex at $(h,k)$ are\n\n$$\nx-h=2pt,\\,y-k=p{t}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is constant.\n\nIn our case, $(h,k)=(1,3),$ and so we have\n\n$$\nx-1=2pt,\\,y-3=p{t}^{2}.\n$$\n\nSince the parabola passes through $(-1,4),$ we can substitute $x=-1$ and $y=4$ into the parametric equations to obtain a system of equations. This gives\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-2=2pt \\\\ 1=p{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the first equation for $t,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2 & =2pt \\\\ t & =-\\frac{1}{p}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the second equation and solving for $p,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & =p{(-\\frac{1}{p})}^{2} \\\\ 1 & =p\\cdot \\frac{1}{{p}^{2}} \\\\ 1 & =\\frac{1}{p} \\\\ p & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the parabola are\n\n$$\nx-1=2(1)t,\\,y-3=(1){t}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhich simplify to\n\n$$\nx-1=2t,\\,y-3={t}^{2}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-84828/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "61e9c047-0bbf-560d-b803-87703164db5b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-84828"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-84821/selection/3fe4322b1b6ffc54a2eb9da85aa3fd3c1ec2c4fe9d34d964e5a11db653efff23" :answer/id #uuid "2a097a16-8ddf-52c7-a590-ae96ec43f4e9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x-1=-3t,\\,y-2=-\\frac{3}{2}{t}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-84821/selection/4a8d332c1847c4b21404370e67f6fdb3edf92a1078699ea7f0bfc1ed727d77e2" :answer/id #uuid "5713448a-87f0-5942-a275-4f1cd9aaf1d4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x+1=-\\frac{4}{3}t,\\,y+2=-\\frac{2}{3}{t}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-84821/selection/95a95bc245e475c1e7e4e40d3a9fe3894e7c2479ed07d93131bb39a51ff222e9" :answer/id #uuid "9305d5cc-2022-5d4f-b678-b75458e98e03" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x-1=-\\frac{3}{2}t,\\,y-2=-\\frac{3}{2}{t}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-84821/selection/ca29cda08dcad84927c5e421c7427f0880a96f41c0230c961e6c0fe1e6aa416e" :answer/id #uuid "f716a89c-c284-50cc-9c82-ba1826cd4167" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x-1=-\\frac{4}{3}t,\\,y-2=-\\frac{2}{3}{t}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-84821/selection/76b8bcecd3d8af27f6aa94bd2ea1a26aaf357f309ab18d78514f38c63dc8c95c" :answer/id #uuid "d3243e97-179a-552a-8f26-a1af3dedb265" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x+1=-3t,\\,y+2=-\\frac{3}{2}{t}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-84821/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "545cf95e-06ea-56fe-a594-ff692f74aec8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-84821/selection/3fe4322b1b6ffc54a2eb9da85aa3fd3c1ec2c4fe9d34d964e5a11db653efff23" :answer-field/choices ["q-84821/selection/3fe4322b1b6ffc54a2eb9da85aa3fd3c1ec2c4fe9d34d964e5a11db653efff23" "q-84821/selection/4a8d332c1847c4b21404370e67f6fdb3edf92a1078699ea7f0bfc1ed727d77e2" "q-84821/selection/95a95bc245e475c1e7e4e40d3a9fe3894e7c2479ed07d93131bb39a51ff222e9" "q-84821/selection/ca29cda08dcad84927c5e421c7427f0880a96f41c0230c961e6c0fe1e6aa416e" "q-84821/selection/76b8bcecd3d8af27f6aa94bd2ea1a26aaf357f309ab18d78514f38c63dc8c95c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-84821" :question/id #uuid "14a70bce-c4a4-5acc-ac6d-0383921a9b0d" :question/math-academy-id "q-84821" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041015/assets/91500faad34245d5b2389ae71aa39f34b10b9a75b1b75307b5aa6231b311307b.png)\n\nWhich of the following sets of parametric equations, defined for $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),$ generate the parabola shown above?" :question/worked-solution "The diagram shows that the parabola is vertical, has its vertex at $(1,2),$ and passes through the point $(7,-4).$\n\nThe parametric equations of a vertical parabola that has its vertex at $(h,k)$ are\n\n$$\nx-h=2pt,\\,y-k=p{t}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is constant.\n\nIn our case, $(h,k)=(1,2),$ and so we have\n\n$$\nx-1=2pt,\\,y-2=p{t}^{2}.\n$$\n\nSince the parabola passes through $(7,-4),$ we can substitute $x=7$ and $y=-4$ into the parametric equations to obtain a system of equations. This gives\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}6=2pt \\\\ -6=p{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the first equation for $t,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6 & =2pt \\\\ t & =\\frac{3}{p}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the second equation and solving for $p,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-6 & =p{(\\frac{3}{p})}^{2} \\\\ -6 & =p\\cdot \\frac{9}{{p}^{2}} \\\\ -6 & =\\frac{9}{p} \\\\ p & =-\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the parabola are\n\n$$\nx-1=2(-\\frac{3}{2})t,\\,y-2=(-\\frac{3}{2}){t}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhich simplify to\n\n$$\nx-1=-3t,\\,y-2=-\\frac{3}{2}{t}^{2}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-84821/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "61e9c047-0bbf-560d-b803-87703164db5b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-84821"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-84842/selection/79e2ba7b035f4a61689325ac6ab3af6fed3469980804cca4dc6aeac85e83a1f8" :answer/id #uuid "6daa4abe-4ca9-5198-82b7-01d76b078024" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x+3=-\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2},\\,y+1=-\\frac{1}{2}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-84842/selection/d33f2af4fe821bf36bec7b6b369604ddb44cccd0b386087438d2b8109a872718" :answer/id #uuid "9e016e23-f067-5f42-adf8-de94c24af360" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x+3=-2{t}^{2},\\,y+1=-4t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-84842/selection/daf802a3419e9ffabffbd6a013076b0e3e12b9ecf9bae7ead5cd112907a813a1" :answer/id #uuid "a0dc9526-9759-5a8d-99ba-f52ca3e1c07f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x-3=-\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2},\\,y-1=-t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-84842/selection/50e94d79ae84835786594d5a8a24a46394415d432ab2d2f31556faced13bb8e6" :answer/id #uuid "668b71eb-4d27-5add-b663-e98d9703dc8f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x-3=-\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2},\\,y-1=-\\frac{1}{2}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-84842/selection/482994c3658de2347fb004d295ac4a7522f8fc29bc44b132d211397690702cac" :answer/id #uuid "f5cfbb25-241e-55fa-a7d4-89ae164d5aaf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x+3=-\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2},\\,y+1=-t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-84842/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "88f24eaa-bd31-5c6c-80a0-5608034660ab" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-84842/selection/482994c3658de2347fb004d295ac4a7522f8fc29bc44b132d211397690702cac" :answer-field/choices ["q-84842/selection/79e2ba7b035f4a61689325ac6ab3af6fed3469980804cca4dc6aeac85e83a1f8" "q-84842/selection/d33f2af4fe821bf36bec7b6b369604ddb44cccd0b386087438d2b8109a872718" "q-84842/selection/daf802a3419e9ffabffbd6a013076b0e3e12b9ecf9bae7ead5cd112907a813a1" "q-84842/selection/50e94d79ae84835786594d5a8a24a46394415d432ab2d2f31556faced13bb8e6" "q-84842/selection/482994c3658de2347fb004d295ac4a7522f8fc29bc44b132d211397690702cac"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-84842" :question/id #uuid "81c9b11f-76b1-5474-bb7c-bc45490a8350" :question/math-academy-id "q-84842" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041015/assets/7cb71517fe60c9d15b6cacddbf5f91c2e4a60103b8917a4d9baa287517a5fd54.png)\n\nWhich of the following sets of parametric equations, defined for $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),$ generate the parabola shown above?" :question/worked-solution "The diagram shows that the parabola is horizontal, has its vertex at $(-3,-1),$ and passes through the point $(-5,1).$\n\nThe parametric equations of a horizontal parabola that has its vertex at $(h,k)$ are\n\n$$\nx-h=p{t}^{2},\\,y-k=2pt,\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is constant.\n\nIn our case, $(h,k)=(-3,-1),$ and so we have\n\n$$\nx+3=p{t}^{2},\\,y+1=2pt.\n$$\n\nSince the parabola passes through $(-5,1),$ we can substitute $x=-5$ and $y=1$ into the parametric equations to obtain a system of equations. This gives\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-2=p{t}^{2} \\\\ 2=2pt.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the second equation for $t,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 & =2pt \\\\ 1 & =pt \\\\ t & =\\frac{1}{p}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the first equation and solving for $p,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2 & =p{(\\frac{1}{p})}^{2} \\\\ -2 & =p\\cdot \\frac{1}{{p}^{2}} \\\\ -2 & =\\frac{1}{p} \\\\ p & =-\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the parabola are\n\n$$\nx+3=(-\\frac{1}{2}){t}^{2},\\,y+1=2(-\\frac{1}{2})t,\n$$\n\nwhich simplify to\n\n$$\nx+3=-\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2},\\,y+1=-t.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-84842/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "337be080-59df-51bf-b0d5-14dba139b9c0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-84842"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-84843"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041015/assets/ba3d2c8719c97911d2339548f08601b07bcfe555d59dbb058a157836c45a34fe.png)\n\nWhich of the following sets of parametric equations, defined for $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),$ generate the parabola shown above?" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-84840"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041015/assets/0d278fe1bf34cd60877be6886c90e1734fab7433f9f94ad7765d379e69c2da42.png)\n\nWhich of the following sets of parametric equations, defined for $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),$ generate the parabola shown above?" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-84844/selection/8243175efe6788dc96bacd15a80322b26c1794090a00ac97a5fa9a779dafa51d" :answer/id #uuid "24e4195f-4961-58a3-ad6d-927d4d45b309" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x-5=-3{t}^{2},\\,y-3=-6t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-84844/selection/8832b16dcb652745b5c838b22026b511b10d15acb4aaef70de7788d3826d4eda" :answer/id #uuid "d57b6a3b-d091-5774-918e-c8541446559a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x-5=-3{t}^{2},\\,y-3=3t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-84844/selection/0085c5ba810c39837dad90c0bb19e1e35c3ab6fecb0706051a754609f0a27bc3" :answer/id #uuid "d42de3a7-da1a-503b-8937-62a5db43cc2e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x-5=3{t}^{2},\\,y-3=-12t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-84844/selection/cdba8a5dd362a887563f8f40e55768b9714f398d9fbe2cfec5fcf2414fefdfb6" :answer/id #uuid "f6108aff-0558-5ff8-8ea2-e84e8090de7b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x+5=-4{t}^{2},\\,y+3=12t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-84844/selection/8dc774d44ccad79be46a05898c1f96c7b0b1a702509b2e0763361fe593b46330" :answer/id #uuid "4ed46ce7-b5e3-5fce-957f-c49ee73a0249" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x+5=-{t}^{2},\\,y+3=6t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-84844/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "010cbe17-2fb0-5d20-8c1d-0e8c93c87267" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-84844/selection/8243175efe6788dc96bacd15a80322b26c1794090a00ac97a5fa9a779dafa51d" :answer-field/choices ["q-84844/selection/8243175efe6788dc96bacd15a80322b26c1794090a00ac97a5fa9a779dafa51d" "q-84844/selection/8832b16dcb652745b5c838b22026b511b10d15acb4aaef70de7788d3826d4eda" "q-84844/selection/0085c5ba810c39837dad90c0bb19e1e35c3ab6fecb0706051a754609f0a27bc3" "q-84844/selection/cdba8a5dd362a887563f8f40e55768b9714f398d9fbe2cfec5fcf2414fefdfb6" "q-84844/selection/8dc774d44ccad79be46a05898c1f96c7b0b1a702509b2e0763361fe593b46330"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-84844" :question/id #uuid "0b6384ed-5b0e-577c-a6f0-3fed248e922b" :question/math-academy-id "q-84844" :question/problem "Which of the following sets of parametric equations, defined for $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),$ generate the horizontal parabola given by the Cartesian equation $(y-3)^{2}=-12(x-5)?$" :question/worked-solution "The parametric equations of a horizontal parabola $(y-k)^{2}=4p(x-h)$ that has its vertex at $(h,k)$ are\n\n$$\nx-h=p{t}^{2},\\,y-k=2pt,\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is constant.\n\nComparing the given Cartesian equation with the general case $(y-k)^{2}=4p(x-h),$ we see that the parabola has its vertex at $(h,k)=(5,3).$ So we have\n\n$$\nx-5=p{t}^{2},\\,y-3=2pt.\n$$\n\nNow, comparing the right-hand sides of the given Cartesian equation and the general case, then solving for $p,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4p(x-h) & =-12(x-5) \\\\ 4p(x-5) & =-12(x-5) \\\\ 4p & =-12 \\\\ p & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the parabola are\n\n$$\nx-5=(-3){t}^{2},\\,y-3=2(-3)t,\n$$\n\nwhich simplify to\n\n$$\nx-5=-3{t}^{2},\\,y-3=-6t.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-84844/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "337be080-59df-51bf-b0d5-14dba139b9c0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-84844"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-106461/selection/d3520f7bc515472e951c4720c0b4b07bce177d833fd438d2de11b23fadfbe910" :answer/id #uuid "5d878cd8-ea9d-571e-b2c4-2747cdeb4e68" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x+4=2t,\\,\\,y+4={t}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106461/selection/866167cfc5f53b8287c63f40e26c18611287837c00c04fa11837398ab9ecf38b" :answer/id #uuid "65732b42-6809-5a6d-8d75-341d87c88a0c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x-4={t}^{2},\\,\\,y-4=2t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106461/selection/851a89cc79c9db04d4625f9023047fab1de852ab8230916d3ddd114fc7a3266c" :answer/id #uuid "1b885b18-3e83-562e-aa15-bede595287dc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x-4=2t,\\,\\,y-4={t}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106461/selection/8cbb2e0128f9f94d4f20b2740f72ebca5522303aa787b58859588f2d06e9ef0d" :answer/id #uuid "eaf074c0-d547-57da-90fc-af45742a3986" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x-4=2{t}^{2},\\,\\,y-4=4t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106461/selection/f651836e6dd85eed219f4cfca6d1645a77dc749ef9cf4718f3bdd6a71ddabdc0" :answer/id #uuid "5aebc749-f346-5867-826e-d05adad1e8d5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x+4={t}^{2},\\,\\,y+4=2t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106461/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "1938660b-7d05-579b-9d0b-397ac95ff0de" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-106461/selection/866167cfc5f53b8287c63f40e26c18611287837c00c04fa11837398ab9ecf38b" :answer-field/choices ["q-106461/selection/d3520f7bc515472e951c4720c0b4b07bce177d833fd438d2de11b23fadfbe910" "q-106461/selection/866167cfc5f53b8287c63f40e26c18611287837c00c04fa11837398ab9ecf38b" "q-106461/selection/851a89cc79c9db04d4625f9023047fab1de852ab8230916d3ddd114fc7a3266c" "q-106461/selection/8cbb2e0128f9f94d4f20b2740f72ebca5522303aa787b58859588f2d06e9ef0d" "q-106461/selection/f651836e6dd85eed219f4cfca6d1645a77dc749ef9cf4718f3bdd6a71ddabdc0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-106461" :question/id #uuid "14e2d3b4-1c1a-54b9-9aa2-2d7f1398ec81" :question/math-academy-id "q-106461" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041015/assets/e5c7f025b6f12599a4ecb5fa0cc9e657fd0b67deb1e50231673113f337ca7776.png)\n\nWhich of the following sets of parametric equations, defined for $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),$ generate the parabola shown above?" :question/worked-solution "The diagram shows that the parabola is horizontal, has its vertex at $(4,4),$ and passes through the point $(8,8).$\n\nThe parametric equations of a horizontal parabola that has its vertex at $(h,k)$ are\n\n$$\nx-h=p{t}^{2},\\,y-k=2pt,\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is constant.\n\nIn our case, $(h,k)=(4,4),$ and so we have\n\n$$\nx-4=p{t}^{2},\\,y-4=2pt.\n$$\n\nSince the parabola passes through $(8,8),$ we can substitute $x=8$ and $y=8$ into the parametric equations to obtain a system of equations. This gives\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}4=p{t}^{2} \\\\ 4=2pt.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the second equation for $t,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4 & =2pt \\\\ 2 & =pt \\\\ t & =\\frac{2}{p}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the first equation and solving for $p,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4 & =p{(\\frac{2}{p})}^{2} \\\\ 4 & =p\\cdot \\frac{4}{{p}^{2}} \\\\ 4 & =\\frac{4}{p} \\\\ p & =\\frac{4}{4} \\\\ p & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the parabola are\n\n$$\nx-4=(1){t}^{2},\\,y-4=2(1)t,\n$$\n\nwhich simplify to\n\n$$\nx-4={t}^{2},\\,y-4=2t.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-106461/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "337be080-59df-51bf-b0d5-14dba139b9c0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-106461"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-84858/selection/465f57bcfd5c0a5b5c7de17005c63c31f128051f34c8741308c12f26fc3a216a" :answer/id #uuid "f5397c54-8139-5733-8580-a4f79904c1a5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(y+1)^{2}=-8(x+4)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-84858/selection/b99ad35bc21cc7ff5c845f409a491aeaae3fcca5da41e25f3cd1ce4227077537" :answer/id #uuid "eb305ccf-145b-5207-8bd6-bdc9122f300d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(y-1)^{2}=-8(x-4)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-84858/selection/bf687b5a2d1f710288191742f15f1a375783c20f0f4f2fea6460c39f14d569a8" :answer/id #uuid "ba9e5623-3783-565e-919b-bb799b142bdb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(y-1)^{2}=-4(x-4)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-84858/selection/538198ff6f600ffd8c984c40a1c2d83434d1af76bf630df99c070dce9d86a543" :answer/id #uuid "46c5c08d-b65f-5780-b59b-90ab99b37d09" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(y-1)^{2}=8(x-4)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-84858/selection/af3b1a0fe54d1a5e4dd4364522e47e5b774ff4230fbfd59e0ca29311817fdae6" :answer/id #uuid "87e44316-19fe-540a-8356-0d990c5e2313" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(y+1)^{2}=4(x+4)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-84858/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e49ae9ed-1279-5d35-9aee-1192b1b696a2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-84858/selection/b99ad35bc21cc7ff5c845f409a491aeaae3fcca5da41e25f3cd1ce4227077537" :answer-field/choices ["q-84858/selection/465f57bcfd5c0a5b5c7de17005c63c31f128051f34c8741308c12f26fc3a216a" "q-84858/selection/b99ad35bc21cc7ff5c845f409a491aeaae3fcca5da41e25f3cd1ce4227077537" "q-84858/selection/bf687b5a2d1f710288191742f15f1a375783c20f0f4f2fea6460c39f14d569a8" "q-84858/selection/538198ff6f600ffd8c984c40a1c2d83434d1af76bf630df99c070dce9d86a543" "q-84858/selection/af3b1a0fe54d1a5e4dd4364522e47e5b774ff4230fbfd59e0ca29311817fdae6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-84858" :question/id #uuid "86db9fdb-2ad8-540e-aac1-953ec9683685" :question/math-academy-id "q-84858" :question/problem "Find the Cartesian equation of the parabola defined by the parametric equations\n\n$$\nx-4=-2{t}^{2},\\,y-1=-4t,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's make $t$ the subject of the parametric equations. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2} & =-\\frac{x-4}{2},\\,t=-\\frac{y-1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSquaring both sides of the second equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2} & ={(-\\frac{y-1}{4})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{16}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now eliminate the parameter $t$ by substituting the above into the equation ${t}^{2}=-\\frac{x-4}{2}$ and rearranging to find the Cartesian equation of the parabola, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{16} & =-\\frac{x-4}{2} \\\\ (y-1)^{2} & =16\\cdot (-\\frac{x-4}{2}) \\\\ (y-1)^{2} & =-8(x-4).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-84858/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "14079b03-66c0-5657-8909-a7d5ea35bfc0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-84858"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-84469"] :question/problem "Find the Cartesian equation of the parabola defined by the parametric equations\n\n$$\nx-6=3t,\\,y-3=\\frac{3}{2}{t}^{2},\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's make $t$ the subject of the parametric equations. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}t & =\\frac{x-6}{3},\\,{t}^{2}=\\frac{2(y-3)}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSquaring both sides of the first equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2} & ={(\\frac{x-6}{3})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(x-6)^{2}}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now eliminate the parameter $t$ by substituting the above into the equation ${t}^{2}=\\frac{2(y-3)}{3}$ and rearranging to find the Cartesian equation of the parabola, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-6)^{2}}{9} & =\\frac{2(y-3)}{3} \\\\ (x-6)^{2} & =9\\cdot (\\frac{2(y-3)}{3}) \\\\ (x-6)^{2} & =6(y-3).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-84853/selection/b9d6f96e749d804043f4f4a556d01039494db6075b2313c6722dc901df021980" :answer/id #uuid "0d83e47e-f5a8-5692-9328-8b1dbf49f1ec" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(y+4)^{2}=2(x-3)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-84853/selection/37962e2ab4c7bda034296512304c0d40e001fd6e796f26bef60cca702d9c7cdb" :answer/id #uuid "837f3d92-4f98-5a73-8554-2b46459a5a67" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(y-4)^{2}=8(x+3)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-84853/selection/359f3df5e544ae53cc3de46c387590d4032bed8466c95f3b02d44267d07c1929" :answer/id #uuid "8abf969a-44a9-5a46-89c7-c62aacde1abe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(y+4)^{2}=8(x-3)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-84853/selection/01459195d37f4b7e865f0463719c6d83a66426b0e9e9bec6c4af7585d0294ff7" :answer/id #uuid "15807e4f-e2b3-5836-9e8c-3f816ab663d9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(y-4)^{2}=16(x+3)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-84853/selection/23dc04ce074f7dff17b56d6f0ef5812e9c55716beafced528ece3956fd47d1f1" :answer/id #uuid "26306e22-7b41-5a1d-a185-58ae76b495f7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(y-4)^{2}=2(x+3)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-84853/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "9d9b3bd0-0efd-5dd5-8533-fc68bb1b1ce9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-84853/selection/37962e2ab4c7bda034296512304c0d40e001fd6e796f26bef60cca702d9c7cdb" :answer-field/choices ["q-84853/selection/b9d6f96e749d804043f4f4a556d01039494db6075b2313c6722dc901df021980" "q-84853/selection/37962e2ab4c7bda034296512304c0d40e001fd6e796f26bef60cca702d9c7cdb" "q-84853/selection/359f3df5e544ae53cc3de46c387590d4032bed8466c95f3b02d44267d07c1929" "q-84853/selection/01459195d37f4b7e865f0463719c6d83a66426b0e9e9bec6c4af7585d0294ff7" "q-84853/selection/23dc04ce074f7dff17b56d6f0ef5812e9c55716beafced528ece3956fd47d1f1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-84853" :question/id #uuid "58efaf59-7cd7-5488-89c6-5996c028fb1d" :question/math-academy-id "q-84853" :question/problem "Find the Cartesian equation of the parabola defined by the parametric equations\n\n$$\nx+3=2{t}^{2},\\,y-4=4t,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's make $t$ the subject of the parametric equations. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2} & =\\frac{x+3}{2},\\,t=\\frac{y-4}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSquaring both sides of the second equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2} & ={(\\frac{y-4}{4})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(y-4)^{2}}{16}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now eliminate the parameter $t$ by substituting the above into the equation ${t}^{2}=\\frac{x+3}{2}$ and rearranging to find the Cartesian equation of the parabola, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(y-4)^{2}}{16} & =\\frac{x+3}{2} \\\\ (y-4)^{2} & =16\\cdot (\\frac{x+3}{2}) \\\\ (y-4)^{2} & =8(x+3).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-84853/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "14079b03-66c0-5657-8909-a7d5ea35bfc0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-84853"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-7446"] :question/problem "What set of parametric equations, defined for $t\\in(-\\infty, \\infty),$ generates the parabola shown below?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041015/assets/1a75a5242f3636efac8def7fc62458e1c1c6972ca79a1ab6fd73af47be622a7a.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-7447"] :question/problem "What set of parametric equations, defined for $t\\in(-\\infty,\\infty),$ generates the parabola shown below?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041015/assets/8355891fbc605593a32dd100ee8c1c2e4324da0630755984158ec23f6d419ab9.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
